00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  I retired a few years ago I had done  25-year service with Tangerine District  Council as a local government officer so  it seemed right that I could take that  experience and that knowledge and take  that into being a counselor  also when my husband and I moved to  Sudbury 22 years ago and we just fell in  love with the area and we wanted to put  something back into it so being a  counselor seeing the obvious choice so I  became a counselor because I found that  I was really passionate about my  community but there were several several  areas where I know people had strong  feelings so antisocial behavior issues  around development things like roads not  being sweet and those sorts of things  and I think it was one of those  situations where you can either sit on  the sidelines and do nothing and  complain or you can literally roll up  your sleeves and get involved so from my  perspective it was something that's very  easy to do everyone comes at it with a  different perspective and especially  what I found quite powerful was that  there are so few young counselors so  they tend to be of a particular age  similar background and actually I think  it was really quite interesting watching  people's reactions saying oh here's  someone who's a little bit younger than  the most local councilors but actually  really cared about their local area and  wants to make it a better place to live  and work I'm a counselor because I was  involved in my community and I wanted to  do more  I was uh on the parish council  um involved in the local church involved  in local business you know I just  enjoy meeting people speaking to them  and trying to help them out where I can  to start with I thought oh no no I can't  possibly do that and then I thought  I don't know there's an awful lot of men  and there's an awful lot of people  traditionally doing it  um so I said oh okay  and I didn't win  I lost about a handful of votes  so obviously when the next session came  round  I thought  so many people had voted for me and I'd  obviously give me the confidence to go  ahead and do it properly which I did and  that time one with a really good  majority so I fell into being a  counselor and people said we are quite  good at this you should do that and  sometimes you think yes I could do that  I stood to make a difference I stood to  make a point I stood to achieve things  that I feel strongly about other kind of  counselor because when I started as a  parish counselor I could see a need at  the district level  and so I put my name forward it was as  simple as that so you're serving you  serve your community which was what my  aim was I got there and I found I'm not  just serving my community but I'm  serving all the communities across the  district  uh helping people with problems casework  we call it you know getting their bins  emptied helping them with the planning  application those sort of things you can  actually make a real difference to  someone and um yeah those are the things  I'm proud of so I had the opportunity  after 35 years of Labor not building or  acquiring new homes we set up a policy  we delivered on a policy that enabled us  to do exactly that so after the last  five years we have actually delivered an  additional  238 homes to provide a house for  somebody that's in need  when my Village lost its shop and its  post office  and the village was what do we do now  and then  I went to my Council and I said you've  got some you've got a small  accommodation  that nobody uses  could I have it please  could I have it for a community shop and  a post office  which they leased to us I mean it's run  by volunteers we needed it to be a safe  place for the Post Office  and I'm thrilled to say that that's now  been going probably 15 years  as a as a local Ward member I represent  five individual villagers and there are  some things that they're very easy to  overlook or ignore if you're a larger  sort of corporate body or entity but  it's things like fixing the roof of a  village hall helping with some speeding  issues on a particular stretch of road  it's a relatively minor things but in  terms of the quality of life for people  living there and that makes a real  difference look government is not just  what's at the top it's local government  Parish councils that's the most  important that's you that's your village  that's your Pub that's your post office  and that's where we need good people and  it's so important because if they like  it and they're good  and they get re-elected then they can  move upwards we need to see a wider  range of people becoming counselors and  you know to be frank a lot of us are a  male pale and stale you know so we need  some younger folk we need people from  different backgrounds who can bring you  know diversity of use to the council and  and perhaps reflect to The Wider Society  we need we need a wide range of people  it's just simply because that's what  Society is  I would definitely like to see more  young people I'd like to see a lot more  diversity amongst the councilors  really really important actually and the  younger people become counselors just  because it is a different perspective I  mean I've seen numerous occasions where  there'll be certain viewpoints certain  perspectives that I haven't been  understood or be misrepresented or  perhaps where the sort of younger voice  and a younger person's perspective isn't  necessarily being given the weight that  I think it should  and it's easy to learn the more effort  you put in the more you get out of it  and the more your community and all the  communities get out of it look for a  place that you can do it a good place to  start and I would recommend this to  anybody in a rural area that just  parishes is to try a parish council few  years ago the Town Council we we joined  a we participated in a shadow in a  counselor scheme it's a central  government scheme so we took we had four  students  and they each had they were assigned one  counselor and they would shadow that  counselor for six months and then it was  great because then they went to London  to get their certificates the house  Department it was fantastic and one of  those young councilors actually stood  for Town Council at a later date to  become a town councilor if you feel  strongly about an issue like I do about  environmental issues that's an  opportunity then to make a difference  come in and help steer your community  and the districts in a slightly  different direction  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

